.TH FBC-WII 1 "May 2026" "FreeBASIC" "FreeBASIC Manual"
.SH NAME
fbc-wii \- FreeBASIC compiler driver for Nintendo Wii homebrew
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbc-wii
.RI [ options ] " file.bas"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbc-wii
is a wrapper around the FreeBASIC compiler configured for the Nintendo Wii
homebrew target.  It selects the Wii target, the PowerPC GCC backend, the
FreeBASIC Wii headers and libraries, and the libogc/devkitPPC toolchain.
.PP
The driver produces Wii homebrew output using the normal FreeBASIC command
line interface.  It expects devkitPro's Wii toolchain and libogc to be
installed on the build system.
.PP
For games that load files from the current directory,
.B fbc-wii
can also stage a homebrew folder and copy asset files beside the DOL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--bundle " DIR
Create
.IR DIR
and, unless an explicit output path is given, write
.IR DIR/boot.dol .
.TP
.BI "--assets " DIR
Copy the contents of
.IR DIR
beside the DOL after a successful build.
.TP
.BI "-x " FILE
.TQ
.BI "-o " FILE
Forward the FreeBASIC output path.  When
.B --assets
is used without
.B --bundle ,
assets are copied beside
.IR FILE .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEVKITPRO
Root of the devkitPro installation.  Defaults to
.IR /opt/devkitpro .
.TP
.B DEVKITPPC
Root of the devkitPPC toolchain.  Defaults to
.IR $DEVKITPRO/devkitPPC .
.TP
.B FBWII_PREFIX
Installation prefix containing the FreeBASIC Wii files.  Defaults to
.IR /usr .
.TP
.B FBWII_COMPILER
Path to the target-specific compiler executable.
.TP
.B FBWII_INCDIR
Path to the FreeBASIC Wii include directory.
.TP
.B FBWII_LIBDIR
Path to the FreeBASIC Wii runtime library directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbc (1)
.
.\" end of fbc-wii.1
